COMPLETE RNA-SEQ PIPELINE (HISAT2 → ANNOTATION → DEG)
1. Setup Directory
mkdir RNAseq_project && cd RNAseq_project
mkdir raw_data qc trimmed index alignments counts results annotation
mv *.fastq.gz raw_data/
---------------------------
2. Quality Control (FastQC + MultiQC)
Install
sudo apt install fastqc
pip install multiqc
Run
fastqc raw_data/*.fastq.gz -o qc/
multiqc qc/ -o qc/

Per base quality
Adapter contamination
---------------------------
3. Trimming (Trimmomatic)
Install
sudo apt install trimmomatic
Run trimmomatic
(files are already trimmed)
--------------------------
4. Reference Genome & Annotation
Download (Rice example)
wget -P annotation/ https://ftp.ensemblgenomes.ebi.ac.uk/pub/plants/release-58/fasta/oryza_sativa/dna/Oryza_sativa.IRGSP-1.0.dna.toplevel.fa.gz

wget -P annotation/ https://ftp.ensemblgenomes.ebi.ac.uk/pub/plants/release-58/gtf/oryza_sativa/Oryza_sativa.IRGSP-1.0.58.gtf.gz

-- files are already provided (rice.fa and rice.gtf)
--------------------------
5. Build HISAT2 Index
sudo apt install hisat2
hisat2-build rice.fa rice_index
--------------------------
6. Alignment (HISAT2)

hisat2 -p 8 -x rice_index -1 C1_R1.fastq.gz -2 C1_R2.fastq.gz -S C1.sam
hisat2 -p 8 -x rice_index -1 C2_R1.fastq.gz -2 C2_R2.fastq.gz -S C2.sam
hisat2 -p 8 -x rice_index -1 C3_R1.fastq.gz -2 C3_R2.fastq.gz -S C3.sam
hisat2 -p 8 -x rice_index -1 T1_R1.fastq.gz -2 T1_R2.fastq.gz -S T1.sam
hisat2 -p 8 -x rice_index -1 T2_R1.fastq.gz -2 T2_R2.fastq.gz -S T2.sam
hisat2 -p 8 -x rice_index -1 T3_R1.fastq.gz -2 T3_R2.fastq.gz -S T3.sam

mkdir alignments 
transfer the .sam files to that folder
-------------------------
7. Convert SAM → BAM → Sort → Index
sudo apt install samtools
ls alignments
samtools view -bS C1.sam | samtools sort -o C1.bam (individually)
for f in *.sam; do samtools view -bS "$f" | samtools sort -o "${f%.sam}_sorted.bam"; done (at once)
for f in *_sorted.bam; do samtools index "$f"; done (samtools index)
-------------------------
8. Read Counting (FeatureCounts)
sudo apt install subread
featureCounts -T 8 -p -t exon -g gene_id \
-a rice.gtf \
-o counts/gene_counts.txt \
*_sorted.bam 

generated gene_counts.txt should be converted to .csv using excel
--------------------------
9. Differential Expression (DESeq2 in R)
--------------------------
10. Functional Annotation (UniProt + BLAST)
Step 1: Download UniProt
wget https://ftp.uniprot.org/pub/databases/uniprot/current_release/knowledgebase/complete/uniprot_sprot.fasta.gz
gunzip uniprot_sprot.fasta.gz
Step 2: Make BLAST DB
makeblastdb -in uniprot_sprot.fasta -dbtype prot -out uniprot_db
Step 3: BLAST (Protein annotation)
blastx -query annotation/Oryza_sativa.IRGSP-1.0.cdna.all.fa \
-db uniprot_db -out annotation/blast.out \
-evalue 1e-5 -outfmt 6 -num_threads 8
